    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## RM \u00b7 2 \u2014 the ears\n\n**Starts:** every 30s, holding a 25-second Telegram long poll open.\n\nRoutes everything that comes back from `/telegram/updates`:\n- **button taps** \u2192 `/decide` \u2192 `/publish`\n- **plain messages** \u2192 `/chat` \u2192 a job for the office (\"create 5 shorts about horror\")\n\n**Only one poll may run at a time.** Telegram kills overlapping `getUpdates` calls with a 409, and\nthat race silently dropped messages for a day. The gateway now single-flights it and reports a 409 as\na skipped poll rather than an error.\n\nCommands starting with `/` never reach here \u2014 the gateway answers those itself, so the console still\nworks when n8n is the thing that is broken.",
        "height": 364,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "overview-note",
      "name": "What this workflow does",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -520,
        -344
      ]
    },
